setvar intF[1112] = 0
music BGM26B.mp3
delay 120
setvar strS[1000] = "BG304"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
if intA[1000] == 0
	goto s39
fi
goto 40
label s39
setvar strS[1000] = ""
label 40
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 98
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text ..."Done!"
text She falls to the floor as she says the word.
text I don't really understand what it is she's made.
text She sits up.
text ..."Do you know what this is?"
text I shake my head sideways.
text ..."A tool to let you hop up in the air."
text I tilt my head to the side, confused.
text ..."Just come over here and get on this."
text I don't even know where I should climb onto.
text The entire thing is slanted, after all.
text As I stand there, she picks me up and then places me on top of the tilted plank.
text ..."You need to hold on to this, or else you really will go flying."
text I grab the handle in front of me.
text ..."Okay."
text She goes around to the other side, before sitting down just like me.
text When she does, my body floats up into the air.
text Now she's below where I am.
text She stretches her legs.
text Now our positions reverse.
text She does this over and over.
text My world rises and sinks.
text She laughs as her hair flies through the air and covers her face.
text ..."Isn't this fun?"
text I nod.
text Most of all, I'm happy that she and I are able to make something this fun together.
text I may have been scared at times, but I'm truly glad it's ended up this way.
text ..."Can we start making something else too?"
text She makes the suggestion to me.
text ..."You'll help me again, won't you?"
text Of course.
setvar strS[1000] = "KURO"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
if intA[1000] == 0
	goto s40
fi
goto 41
label s40
setvar strS[1000] = ""
label 41
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 98
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text We continue in the same way, gathering junk and creating toys.
text By the time I realize it, the space in front of our home has become a playground.
text Finally, we create a lookout that sits high in the sky.
setvar strS[1000] = "BG310"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
if intA[1000] == 0
	goto s41
fi
goto 42
label s41
setvar strS[1000] = ""
label 42
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 98
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text I sit on top of her legs and, together, we look down at the ground.
text I see the playground we built for the two of us and no one else.
text It looks so desolate from here.
text And at the same time, I recall why the world within my memories felt so warm:
text It was full of people.
text I look up at her.
text ..."Hm?"
text She looks down at me, puzzled.
text Does she know everything?
text Does she live here having accepted it all?
text And did it have to be her?
text Or did it just happen to be her?
text In either case, how could this world be any sadder?
text How could she love this world?
text If not for me, she would be completely alone.
text She was by herself the whole time until I was born...
text What was her life like then?
text How did she spend her days?
text What could she have been thinking...
text Living in a world as depressing as this one?
text ..."What's wrong?"
text She asks me a question.
text ..."Do you feel like crying?"
text I nod.
text ..."Did you remember something sad?"
text No.
text What's sad is everything.
text All of it is tragic.
text This place can't tolerate the existence of those with hearts.
text This is wrong.
text This place ought to have been left behind and forgotten by everyone and everything.
text I look out to the edges of the world.
text The world's end.
text It's filled with a lamenting color.
text And this is where I will come to an end.
text I will be reaching my end here for eternity.
text She must have realized it long ago.
text 　...Was that what you sought...?
text 　...To be born in this place?
text That's why she asked me that question when I first looked at the outside world.
text The sky is the only thing here that stretches out across everything.
text Looking at it makes me think... Perhaps there's an end to be found at its tip.
text Or perhaps that is the world where I once was.
text ..."If only we could cry."
text I stare into the sky as she holds me in her arms.
text If this sky were connected to another, separate world...
text I'd want to take her there.
text But how...?
text I search within my heart for a way.
text But... I'm unable to come up with a single idea.
text The smell of the wind seems to have changed.
text It's the first time this has happened since I was born here.
text Her arm holds me even tighter.
text She must have noticed too.
text ..."So even this world... has a winter."
text She says the words as she keeps her eyes fixed on the same spot.
music ~
